    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0209" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./66: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-06-08T12:00:00+03:00">June 8,
                            1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 8—8:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. Your 108, June 6, 4 p.m. I shall see Krestinsky tomorrow and then reply fully. Until I can report
                        Krestinsky’s views I believe that it
                    would be inadvisable for the Department to negotiate with Troyanovsky who may or may not represent the
                    point of view of his Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
